ight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;14,007&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;15,623&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Accruals for property, plant and equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;453&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;896&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;12.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Transactions with Related Parties&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's costs of doing business are reflected in the financial statements for the period presented. These costs include direct charges and allocations from related parties for (1) project development costs subject to the Company's overall management, supervision, and (2) control engineering, cost estimation, expansion flow studies, and other various construction and project management services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company had also contracted, subject to the Company's overall management, supervision, and control, to provide certain operation and maintenance services including, but not limited to, business services, preparing financial statements, tax returns, and other various accounting functions as defined in the Company's Amended and Restated Operations and Maintenance Agreement dated January 1, 2020 (Operating Agreement). The Operating Agreement was in effect through December 31, 2023, and was renewed year to year thereafter. In 2025, notice was provided by TransCanada Northern Border Inc. (TCNB) to terminate the Operating Agreement effective December 31, 2025. TCNB will provide Termination Assistance Services and continue to serve as operator of the Company for up to one year after the effective termination date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has a Retained Asset Capacity Agreement with Columbia Gas Transmission, LLC (TCO) earning a total of $5.6 million every year for providing capacity on the Company's pipeline that automatically renews on a year-to-year basis with FERC approval required to terminate the agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;During the normal course of business, the Company earns transportation revenues and incurs transportation expenses with related parties. The following table shows revenues, capital, and expenses from/to the Company's related party entities for the years ended December 31:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:91.964%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:58.285%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:2.388%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:15.081%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:2.388%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:15.081%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.977%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;(In thousands)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:15pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Operating revenues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12,253&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13,842&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Capital expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;374&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;762&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Operation and maintenance expense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7,915&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6,989&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:15pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:6pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;13.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Capital Contributions and Cash Distributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Capital contributions consist of amounts provided by each of the members to fund project development and operating costs. There were no contributions from members in 2025 and a $2.5 million contribution from members in 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company distributed $177.0 million and $186.0 million of earnings in 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;14.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Effective March 30, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; the Millennium Board of Managers authorized a distribution of $45.0 million to members no later than &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;March 30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Subsequent events have been assessed through April&#160;2, 2026, the date the financial statements were issued, and we concluded there were no events or transactions during this period that would require recognition or disclosure in the financial statements other than those already reflected.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;OVERHEADS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Administrative, engineering, and supervision salaries, expenses, and employee benefits relating to construction activities are capitalized based on labor recorded to the payroll system. The amounts so capitalized are directly assigned, based on individual construction projects, exclusive of construction orders covering the cost of capitalized software and purchases of general plant, furniture, transportation equipment, tools, and similar property, on a percentage basis with the same percentage being applied to all types of construction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;ALLOWANCE FOR FUNDS USED DURING CONSTRUCTION (AFUDC):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Computed monthly on construction work in progress, exclusive of construction projects covering the purchase of property normally placed in service when received. The amounts so capitalized are directly assigned, based on individual construction projects exclusive of construction orders covering the purchase of general plant furniture, transportation equipment, tools and similar property, on a percentage basis with the same percentage being applied to all types of construction. In 2025 $120,033.81 of equity and $16,509.01 of debt were directly charged to construction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
  <ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.75pt"&gt;Refer to pages 120, 122, 256, and 258 for information related to debt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock>
